# Tool versions this repo's config was last checked against.
#
#   ./dotctl versions                  drift report (tested vs installed)
#   ./dotctl versions review <tool>    triage the changes now, draft a plan if needed
#   ./dotctl versions accept <tool>    after reviewing: record the installed version
#                                      and sync in-file copies (.tmux.conf
#                                      @target_version, nvim init.lua + README)
#
# Columns (whitespace-separated; probe is the rest of the line):
#   tool     brew formula name when pin is set
#   tested   version the config was checked against
#   checked  date of that check
#   pin      -      not brew-pinned, upgrades whenever brew/the app does
#            exact  brew-pinned, only `dotctl versions upgrade` moves it
#            patch  brew-pinned, the homebrew-update cron may apply patch upgrades
#            minor  brew-pinned, the cron may apply minor and patch upgrades
#   review   auto   the daily versions-review agent triages drift by itself
#            manual tracked only; run `dotctl versions review <tool>` yourself
#   changes  where to read what changed: file path, URL, nvim:help-news,
#            git-log (git log <tested>..HEAD in the checkout the probe names), or
#            lazy-lock (diff of .config/nvim/lazy-lock.json between the commits)
#   probe    command printing the installed version, run from the repo root; the
#            first X.Y[.Z] token (or the first word, cut to 7 chars for a git
#            SHA) is compared
#
# tool                    tested    checked     pin    review  changes                                         probe
tmux                      3.8       2026-10-20  patch  auto    /opt/homebrew/opt/tmux/CHANGES                  tmux -V
neovim                    0.12.6    2026-10-20  patch  auto    nvim:help-news                                  nvim --version
fzf                       0.74.5    2026-10-20  patch  auto    https://github.com/junegunn/fzf/releases        fzf --version
